# Obsidian vault + docs

Treasure Trap has **two** agent-readable design sources. Use both.

## Sources

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `obsidian/` | Granular idea/design notebook: one mechanic per note, MOCs, Inbox, status tags |
| `docs/` and especially `docs/context/` | Compact Cursor router (`INDEX.md`), `HANDOFF.md`, roadmap checklists, implementation ledgers |

## Load order for product / design work

1. `docs/context/INDEX.md` (task router)
2. Relevant area MOC under `obsidian/_MOCs/` (e.g. `MOC - Items & Power-ups.md`)
3. Atomic notes linked from that MOC for the specific mechanic
4. Matching `docs/context/*.md` when you need the compact ledger / checklist
5. Verify implementation claims in code

For brainstorming / meeting outcomes, also check `obsidian/00-Inbox/`.

## Status tags (shared vocabulary)

`LOCKED` · `PILOT` · `IDEA` · `REJECTED` — same meaning in Obsidian frontmatter/tags and `docs/context/STATUS.md`.

Never ship `IDEA` notes without an explicit request to promote them. Never treat `Archive/` or historical root docs as current truth.

## Conflict resolution

1. Latest explicit product-owner decision
2. LOCKED record in `obsidian/` or `docs/context/`
3. Active `.cursor/rules/`
4. Shipped code (implementation truth, not necessarily design truth)
5. `obsidian/Archive/` and older root `docs/` history

## When decisions change

Update the atomic Obsidian note **and** the relevant `docs/context/` file when both apply. Capture raw meeting notes in `obsidian/00-Inbox/` first, then file into atomic notes.

Vault conventions: `obsidian/_meta/Conventions.md` and `obsidian/_meta/How Agents Use This Vault.md`.
